  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Central African Republic (01-Jul-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central African Republic, Malaria, The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC)This program has the following goals: By the end of 2017, 50% reduction in malaria morbidity and mortality in the general population compared to the 2010 level.. The objectives of this program are: At least 80 % of the population adopting adequate behaviors to the fight against malaria by the end of 2017..  Building of capacitites of the Program at all levels (institutional,managerial and technical) by the end of 2017..  Ensure the adequate case management of at least 80% of malaria cases in health facilities and targetted communities by the end of 2017..  Ensure the availability of quality antimalarial drugs and other commodities to at least 80% of the public, private health facilities and targetted communities by the end of 2017..  Protect at least 80 % of the population with effective interventions for the prevention of malaria by the end of 2017..  Strengthen the system of monitoring and evaluation for the detection of outbreaks of malaria cases and operational research by the end of 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
